1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,145
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:07,145 --> 00:00:10,540
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:13,351
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:14,465
Here, eat your star.

5
00:00:14,465 --> 00:00:15,608
You can look at it on your plate for now.

6
00:00:15,608 --> 00:00:17,081
To make up for not getting to see the stars today.

7
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:18,210
What’s that?

8
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:19,859
It’s called a kaleidoscope.

9
00:00:19,859 --> 00:00:22,558
From now on, if you see triangle mirrors like these,

10
00:00:22,558 --> 00:00:24,321
you’ll only think of my face.

11
00:00:24,321 --> 00:00:25,984
We might not get to see the simulated stars,

12
00:00:26,143 --> 00:00:27,694
but we ended up seeing the real ones.

13
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,709
What are you going to do next?

14
00:00:29,709 --> 00:00:31,198
Go home and sleep, nerd.

15
00:00:31,409 --> 00:00:32,858
Can I get a goodnight kiss?

16
00:00:32,858 --> 00:00:33,527
Huh?

17
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:54,973
♪ It’s like this every morning ♪

18
00:01:54,973 --> 00:01:59,267
♪ Waking up and missing you first thing ♪

19
00:01:59,267 --> 00:02:02,863
♪ It’s not because the day is beautiful ♪

20
00:02:02,863 --> 00:02:05,207
♪ It’s just how much my heart loves you ♪
Can I get another goodnight kiss?

21
00:02:08,996 --> 00:02:09,708
Whoa!

22
00:02:28,161 --> 00:02:29,780
Can I hit on you?

23
00:02:32,038 --> 00:02:33,001
When did you get here?

24
00:02:33,001 --> 00:02:33,947
A while ago.

25
00:02:48,355 --> 00:02:50,014
I’m currently hitting on you.

26
00:02:50,843 --> 00:02:52,211
I’m hitting on you.

27
00:02:58,827 --> 00:03:00,463
I’m currently hitting on you.

28
00:03:04,074 --> 00:03:04,916
Damn!

29
00:03:04,916 --> 00:03:06,589
Why do you keep following me everywhere?

30
00:03:16,435 --> 00:03:19,057
Did you know I’m already hitting on you?

31
00:03:55,678 --> 00:03:56,760
Who are you staring at?

32
00:03:59,089 --> 00:04:00,096
Are you seeing things?

33
00:04:10,347 --> 00:04:12,331
Did you know?

34
00:04:14,378 --> 00:04:15,596
I can’t take this anymore!

35
00:04:15,596 --> 00:04:16,973
Hey, it’s me!

36
00:04:20,431 --> 00:04:22,915
I was just going to ask you
what the answer to this question was.

37
00:04:29,579 --> 00:04:30,322
Whoa.

38
00:04:30,446 --> 00:04:32,328
Dude, you almost had to respawn.

39
00:04:33,351 --> 00:04:34,251
Sorry.

40
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:37,382
Is something wrong?

41
00:04:43,952 --> 00:04:45,001
The thing is…

42
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:47,970
I see Cheewa in my mind all the time.

43
00:04:49,399 --> 00:04:50,760
You’ve got it bad.

44
00:04:52,295 --> 00:04:53,249
Are you hallucinating?

45
00:04:53,690 --> 00:04:54,636
Not at first.

46
00:04:55,201 --> 00:04:56,333
But now I’m starting to.

47
00:04:57,409 --> 00:05:00,297
Could it be that the kid put a spell on you?

48
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,715
Damn.

49
00:05:02,103 --> 00:05:04,914
A science kid practicing black magic.

50
00:05:06,131 --> 00:05:07,548
You guys are silly.

51
00:05:07,548 --> 00:05:08,770
It’s nothing like that.

52
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:10,288
It’s probably just an illusion.

53
00:05:11,788 --> 00:05:15,149
Have you seen Cheewa in person today?

54
00:05:15,237 --> 00:05:15,824
Not yet.

55
00:05:16,089 --> 00:05:17,459
He has exams coming up.

56
00:05:17,459 --> 00:05:18,764
He’s probably studying hard right now.

57
00:05:18,764 --> 00:05:20,000
He’s such a Doctor Strange.

58
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,437
One body is reading the Darkhold.

59
00:05:22,437 --> 00:05:24,962
The other splits off and goes into your head.

60
00:05:25,174 --> 00:05:26,519
Damn, that’s so scary.

61
00:05:26,995 --> 00:05:27,739
Damn.

62
00:05:28,321 --> 00:05:30,711
Niran, just throw him already.

63
00:05:30,923 --> 00:05:32,183
I think he’s the craziest one.

64
00:05:32,183 --> 00:05:32,999
I agree.

65
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:33,862
I can fight, you know?

66
00:05:33,862 --> 00:05:34,624
He really is.

67
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:35,829
I’m Ancient One.

68
00:05:35,829 --> 00:05:38,737
Before you two start fighting each other,
let’s tackle these books first.

69
00:05:38,949 --> 00:05:41,632
If you don’t study today, you won’t have
the energy to fight tomorrow.

70
00:05:42,496 --> 00:05:43,718
Oh, I have a headache.

71
00:05:44,441 --> 00:05:45,461
I have a headache.

72
00:05:45,708 --> 00:05:47,244
I have a headache. I don’t want to study.

73
00:05:47,244 --> 00:05:48,501
Looking at all these words
gives me a headache.

74
00:05:48,501 --> 00:05:49,336
Ugh.

75
00:05:49,883 --> 00:05:50,845
Help me, universe.

76
00:05:55,401 --> 00:06:01,816
Illusions.

77
00:06:01,816 --> 00:06:04,986
Illusions aren't caused by damaged
or malfunctioning eyes.

78
00:06:10,526 --> 00:06:11,342
Did you know?

79
00:06:12,665 --> 00:06:15,000
An illusion occurs when the brain is tricked

80
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,426
while processing the information
in front of us

81
00:06:17,973 --> 00:06:19,301
due to many factors,

82
00:06:19,654 --> 00:06:21,066
including physical,

83
00:06:21,066 --> 00:06:23,261
physiological, and cognitive factors.

84
00:06:24,567 --> 00:06:25,614
Are you the real Cheewa?

85
00:06:26,726 --> 00:06:27,416
Yes.

86
00:06:29,781 --> 00:06:32,365
What’s the real him even wearing?

87
00:06:32,577 --> 00:06:33,257
Oh.

88
00:06:33,257 --> 00:06:34,540
It’s a costume from my club.

89
00:06:34,716 --> 00:06:36,200
We had a photoshoot today.

90
00:06:37,382 --> 00:06:38,485
You didn’t think to change back?

91
00:06:39,667 --> 00:06:40,832
You came home wearing that?

92
00:06:41,714 --> 00:06:43,429
Yes, I did.

93
00:06:44,241 --> 00:06:46,446
I wanted to surprise you, P’Niran.

94
00:06:46,852 --> 00:06:48,978
I just want to help
take your mind off your exams.

95
00:07:00,904 --> 00:07:02,929
Oh, it makes a sound?

96
00:07:17,037 --> 00:07:18,433
Wanna take me home and play with me?

97
00:07:22,756 --> 00:07:23,761
Are you sure you’re the real you?

98
00:07:24,343 --> 00:07:27,043
In this case, it’s a physiological factor.

99
00:07:27,043 --> 00:07:30,161
When the eyes and the visual areas
of the brain are overstimulated,

100
00:07:30,372 --> 00:07:33,321
when we look at something for too long,

101
00:07:33,621 --> 00:07:35,266
or see the same image repeatedly,

102
00:07:36,042 --> 00:07:37,875
our neurons retain that image.

103
00:07:38,104 --> 00:07:40,263
Then, when we look away,

104
00:07:40,263 --> 00:07:41,829
the image can linger in our vision.

105
00:07:43,487 --> 00:07:44,245
What does that mean?

106
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:46,164
It means you miss me, P’Niran.

107
00:07:47,205 --> 00:07:49,459
You miss me much more than usual, I guess.

108
00:07:53,976 --> 00:07:54,857
Where have you been today?

109
00:07:54,857 --> 00:07:55,507
I didn’t see you around.

110
00:07:56,619 --> 00:07:59,072
I was studying for the exams with my friends.

111
00:07:59,213 --> 00:08:01,527
And we had a little alien activity.

112
00:08:02,021 --> 00:08:03,373
Most importantly,

113
00:08:04,608 --> 00:08:07,156
I didn’t want to disturb you
while you were studying.

114
00:08:08,408 --> 00:08:09,587
You’ve been disturbing me all day.

115
00:08:10,893 --> 00:08:12,619
I apologize on behalf of the illusions.

116
00:08:17,612 --> 00:08:18,450
You’re annoying.

117
00:08:21,044 --> 00:08:23,021
This alien’s going to head out.

118
00:08:23,233 --> 00:08:26,141
So we can both have more time to study.

119
00:08:26,141 --> 00:08:27,002
Mm.

120
00:08:31,713 --> 00:08:32,610
Wait.

121
00:08:35,609 --> 00:08:36,710
Study hard, okay?

122
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:40,716
You too, P’Niran.

123
00:08:41,069 --> 00:08:43,419
Let’s celebrate after our exams.

124
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,566
Yeah, okay.

125
00:08:51,324 --> 00:08:52,242
Hold on.

126
00:08:53,547 --> 00:08:54,674
Can you help me with something?

127
00:08:55,539 --> 00:08:56,776
I’ve never seen one before.

128
00:08:57,076 --> 00:08:58,754
That alien abduction thing.

129
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,225
But you don’t have to do it.

130
00:09:15,586 --> 00:09:17,155
Is that really Cheewa?

131
00:09:18,002 --> 00:09:19,736
Damn, he’s so funny.

132
00:09:22,541 --> 00:09:23,668
That’s pretty cute, actually.

133
00:09:35,255 --> 00:09:36,239
What was he doing?

134
00:09:45,315 --> 00:09:46,072
Whoa.

135
00:09:46,072 --> 00:09:47,417
Niran’s just feeding you.

136
00:09:47,646 --> 00:09:49,091
Are you really that touched?

137
00:09:49,091 --> 00:09:52,288
I’m worried you won’t be used to
how cool I look.

138
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:11,260
We’re done with exams!

139
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:12,866
I love school breaks.

140
00:10:12,866 --> 00:10:14,546
I love you, baby!

141
00:10:15,003 --> 00:10:16,248
I’ve missed school breaks.

142
00:10:16,248 --> 00:10:17,481
I want to hug it.

143
00:10:17,481 --> 00:10:18,509
But I can’t.

144
00:10:18,509 --> 00:10:20,067
So I guess I’ll hug my friends for now.

145
00:10:20,067 --> 00:10:20,663
Hey.

146
00:10:20,663 --> 00:10:21,751
Whoa.

147
00:10:22,187 --> 00:10:23,536
Hug me too.

148
00:10:23,667 --> 00:10:24,382
No.

149
00:10:26,515 --> 00:10:27,988
Hey, I’m hungry.

150
00:10:29,817 --> 00:10:31,258
Wanna celebrate the end of our exams?

151
00:10:31,998 --> 00:10:32,629
Yeah.

152
00:10:33,478 --> 00:10:34,675
What should we eat?

153
00:10:35,328 --> 00:10:36,077
Hmm…

154
00:10:36,730 --> 00:10:37,711
Pork BBQ?

155
00:10:40,955 --> 00:10:42,532
I’m in. You don’t even have to ask.

156
00:10:42,532 --> 00:10:44,381
I could eat a whole buffalo right now.

157
00:10:44,834 --> 00:10:45,560
Ah.

158
00:10:45,669 --> 00:10:47,190
- Enjoy.
- Enjoy.

159
00:10:47,190 --> 00:10:47,922
Moo~

160
00:10:47,922 --> 00:10:48,577
Hey!

161
00:10:48,577 --> 00:10:50,026
Screw you guys!

162
00:10:50,461 --> 00:10:53,081
Hey, what about Cheewa
and the other two nerds?

163
00:10:53,081 --> 00:10:54,517
They might be celebrating with their class.

164
00:10:55,322 --> 00:10:56,379
Wanna make a bet?

165
00:10:56,379 --> 00:10:59,382
I bet Cheewa would definitely want to have
pork BBQ with us.

166
00:10:59,382 --> 00:11:00,834
Loser pays.

167
00:11:00,834 --> 00:11:01,928
Hmm…

168
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:02,875
No, thanks.

169
00:11:02,875 --> 00:11:03,701
I don’t bet.

170
00:11:07,097 --> 00:11:08,135
No more guessing.

171
00:11:08,202 --> 00:11:08,885
There.

172
00:11:09,364 --> 00:11:10,110
He’s coming this way.

173
00:11:13,702 --> 00:11:15,234
How about we bet on something else
about Cheewa?

174
00:11:15,234 --> 00:11:17,814
What’s the first thing he’ll say?

175
00:11:18,242 --> 00:11:19,330
I think he’ll say this.

176
00:11:20,114 --> 00:11:21,944
“Hello, seniors.”

177
00:11:22,722 --> 00:11:24,265
He’ll probably say this.

178
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:26,633
“Were your exams difficult?”

179
00:11:27,330 --> 00:11:28,336
I’d go with

180
00:11:29,033 --> 00:11:31,283
“Hey. Did you know?”

181
00:11:31,283 --> 00:11:32,434
You’re right.

182
00:11:32,434 --> 00:11:33,980
He’s definitely going to win.

183
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:37,589
I’ve heard him say that all day.

184
00:11:38,024 --> 00:11:38,970
What about you, Niran?

185
00:11:38,970 --> 00:11:39,980
What do you think he’s going to say?

186
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:41,037
You guys go ahead.

187
00:11:41,037 --> 00:11:41,742
I’m hungry.

188
00:11:42,404 --> 00:11:43,596
You’re no fun.

189
00:11:43,596 --> 00:11:44,319
Not at all.

190
00:11:48,242 --> 00:11:49,151
I’m hungry.

191
00:11:49,543 --> 00:11:50,441
Damn!

192
00:11:50,441 --> 00:11:51,151
Niran,

193
00:11:51,151 --> 00:11:52,370
how did you know?

194
00:11:53,350 --> 00:11:55,443
Gosh, I’m going crazy.

195
00:11:57,359 --> 00:11:58,324
Let’s go eat.

196
00:11:58,563 --> 00:11:59,405
Do you want to get pork BBQ?

197
00:11:59,732 --> 00:12:00,429
Yes.

198
00:12:00,429 --> 00:12:00,996
Do you?

199
00:12:01,671 --> 00:12:02,509
Follow me.

200
00:12:02,509 --> 00:12:03,144
You lead the way.

201
00:12:03,754 --> 00:12:04,891
Let’s go.

202
00:12:05,261 --> 00:12:06,621
I can’t with my friends.

203
00:12:06,817 --> 00:12:07,867
For God’s sake.

204
00:12:10,022 --> 00:12:12,962
Pork BBQ is very important to humankind.

205
00:12:12,962 --> 00:12:14,298
Without it,

206
00:12:14,298 --> 00:12:16,851
we might just become space debris,

207
00:12:16,851 --> 00:12:17,762
a mass of matter

208
00:12:17,762 --> 00:12:20,716
drifting through space
aimlessly.

209
00:12:21,195 --> 00:12:22,493
Thank you, food,

210
00:12:22,493 --> 00:12:25,404
for nourishing our brain cells
and keeping them working efficiently.

211
00:12:25,404 --> 00:12:27,482
Wait, are you guys like this at every meal?

212
00:12:27,482 --> 00:12:28,478
You guys are only realizing this now?

213
00:12:28,478 --> 00:12:29,192
Oh?

214
00:12:29,192 --> 00:12:30,073
What are they talking about?

215
00:12:30,073 --> 00:12:31,464
Aren’t you used to it by now?

216
00:12:31,464 --> 00:12:32,159
Just eat.

217
00:12:32,573 --> 00:12:33,365
You’re right.

218
00:12:33,922 --> 00:12:35,034
Want some pork, P’Thipok?

219
00:12:35,034 --> 00:12:36,215
You have to cook it for 10 minutes.

220
00:12:36,367 --> 00:12:36,906
This is still raw.

221
00:12:36,906 --> 00:12:37,406
Huh?

222
00:12:37,406 --> 00:12:38,341
Oh, okay.

223
00:12:42,608 --> 00:12:43,902
Cheewa, have some.

224
00:12:43,902 --> 00:12:45,482
We can take turns grilling.

225
00:12:45,482 --> 00:12:46,612
You go ahead.

226
00:12:46,612 --> 00:12:48,242
I want to grill a bunch first.

227
00:12:48,242 --> 00:12:49,271
Just eat. Come on.

228
00:12:49,271 --> 00:12:49,942
Here.

229
00:12:49,942 --> 00:12:50,442
Did you know—

230
00:12:50,442 --> 00:12:51,185
Open your mouth.

231
00:12:51,467 --> 00:12:52,261
Oh.

232
00:12:56,082 --> 00:12:56,908
Mm.

233
00:12:57,713 --> 00:12:58,931
It’s good, right?

234
00:12:59,736 --> 00:13:01,050
Do you like lard?

235
00:13:01,834 --> 00:13:02,538
I can eat it.

236
00:13:02,538 --> 00:13:03,270
You can, right?

237
00:13:03,270 --> 00:13:04,757
You have to eat chili with pork BBQ,
right, Hem?

238
00:13:04,888 --> 00:13:05,482
Yeah.

239
00:13:05,863 --> 00:13:07,072
Let me give him some chili.

240
00:13:07,638 --> 00:13:08,658
Here. Open your mouth.

241
00:13:09,093 --> 00:13:10,688
Oh, that’s good.

242
00:13:10,993 --> 00:13:12,322
Don’t be jealous.

243
00:13:12,627 --> 00:13:13,289
A nice big bite.

244
00:13:13,289 --> 00:13:13,904
That’s enough.

245
00:13:13,904 --> 00:13:14,882
Just a bite.

246
00:13:17,821 --> 00:13:18,668
Whoa.

247
00:13:19,343 --> 00:13:20,628
Niran’s just feeding you.

248
00:13:20,867 --> 00:13:22,383
Are you really that touched?

249
00:13:24,242 --> 00:13:24,996
No, I—

250
00:13:24,996 --> 00:13:25,562
Hey.

251
00:13:25,562 --> 00:13:26,654
Cheewa is having a reaction to the chili.

252
00:13:27,307 --> 00:13:27,944
Hmm?

253
00:13:27,944 --> 00:13:29,282
Parncheewa doesn’t usually eat spicy food.

254
00:13:29,282 --> 00:13:29,978
Shit.

255
00:13:30,892 --> 00:13:31,602
Where's the water?

256
00:13:31,754 --> 00:13:32,565
Bring it here.

257
00:13:32,565 --> 00:13:33,122
Where’s the water?

258
00:13:33,122 --> 00:13:34,162
Why are you only telling us now?

259
00:13:34,162 --> 00:13:34,850
Oh.

260
00:13:35,394 --> 00:13:36,522
No one asked.

261
00:13:36,522 --> 00:13:37,603
So there was no answer.

262
00:13:37,603 --> 00:13:38,406
Ugh!

263
00:13:38,406 --> 00:13:39,266
Goddamn it!

264
00:13:39,362 --> 00:13:40,642
Niran, give him some water now.

265
00:13:40,642 --> 00:13:41,410
Yeah, where’s the water?

266
00:13:41,410 --> 00:13:41,910
Over there!

267
00:13:41,910 --> 00:13:43,000
Come on!

268
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:43,800
Get the jug.

269
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,206
The hose is over there. I saw it.

270
00:13:45,990 --> 00:13:46,980
Are you crazy?

271
00:13:47,285 --> 00:13:48,560
- Hurry. Give him that.
- Open your mouth.

272
00:13:50,672 --> 00:13:52,085
Who drinks an entire jug of water?

273
00:13:52,162 --> 00:13:53,078
You idiot.

274
00:13:53,513 --> 00:13:54,636
Pour it into his cup.

275
00:13:54,636 --> 00:13:55,840
Oh, okay.

276
00:13:56,689 --> 00:13:59,002
Whoa, why didn’t you say anything?

277
00:13:59,002 --> 00:13:59,716
Are you feeling better now?

278
00:14:01,348 --> 00:14:02,522
I mixed way too much chili just now.

279
00:14:02,522 --> 00:14:03,224
I’m feeling better now.

280
00:14:03,224 --> 00:14:04,392
Whoa, he's bright red.

281
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:06,678
Are you blushing because it’s spicy
or because of me?

282
00:14:07,571 --> 00:14:08,616
Because it’s spicy.

283
00:14:10,002 --> 00:14:11,503
Drink some more water.

284
00:14:15,030 --> 00:14:16,629
Oh, no. Your face is all red.

285
00:14:17,456 --> 00:14:18,906
Give him more water.

286
00:14:18,906 --> 00:14:19,948
Okay.

287
00:14:27,493 --> 00:14:28,434
Look.

288
00:14:28,434 --> 00:14:30,282
So much for avoiding it.

289
00:14:30,456 --> 00:14:32,242
What’s wrong, Cheewa?

290
00:14:32,242 --> 00:14:32,989
It’s spicy.

291
00:14:33,076 --> 00:14:33,903
It’s spicy.

292
00:14:34,263 --> 00:14:36,526
Cheers!

293
00:14:37,288 --> 00:14:38,830
We’re done with school.
We don’t have to study anymore.

294
00:14:38,830 --> 00:14:39,575
Hmm?

295
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:42,340
Exams are over. No more classes.

296
00:14:44,995 --> 00:14:46,518
Want some shrimp?

297
00:14:46,518 --> 00:14:47,842
No, I’m allergic to shrimp.

298
00:14:48,081 --> 00:14:50,231
Can I really go in and do judo?

299
00:14:50,470 --> 00:14:52,083
Are you sure you won’t get in trouble?

300
00:14:52,083 --> 00:14:53,005
Of course, you can.

301
00:14:53,005 --> 00:14:54,001
No one will say anything.

302
00:14:54,654 --> 00:14:56,689
The club room is no one’s private property.

303
00:14:57,342 --> 00:14:58,999
If you want to practice, just go in.

304
00:14:59,195 --> 00:15:00,920
We’re actually happy
to have someone interested in judo.

305
00:15:02,574 --> 00:15:03,307
Here.

306
00:15:05,832 --> 00:15:06,810
You can change in the bathroom.

307
00:15:06,810 --> 00:15:08,002
Once you’re done, I’ll see you outside.

308
00:15:08,350 --> 00:15:09,044
Okay.

309
00:15:10,590 --> 00:15:11,653
Let me help you with that.

310
00:15:15,201 --> 00:15:16,313
Just change into the uniform.

311
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,539
You know how to put it on, right?

312
00:15:18,453 --> 00:15:19,141
Yes.

313
00:15:19,141 --> 00:15:19,850
Okay.

314
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:21,472
Wait, P’Niran.

315
00:15:23,301 --> 00:15:25,652
I made a cheer banner.

316
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,242
This is for cheering you on.

317
00:15:31,352 --> 00:15:32,194
How?

318
00:15:34,523 --> 00:15:37,022
If you win, you get a free hug from me.

319
00:15:37,218 --> 00:15:40,192
When you see “Free Hugs,”
you’ll get it right away.

320
00:15:41,759 --> 00:15:43,169
My name’s not even on that.

321
00:15:43,169 --> 00:15:44,404
How would I know you’re cheering me on?

322
00:15:44,404 --> 00:15:46,465
I wouldn’t cheer for anyone else but you.

323
00:15:47,227 --> 00:15:49,878
Because I’m in the process of hitting on you.

324
00:15:56,141 --> 00:15:56,830
Okay.

325
00:15:56,830 --> 00:15:57,556
Go change already.

326
00:15:57,556 --> 00:15:58,469
See you outside. Hurry.

327
00:15:58,861 --> 00:15:59,536
Okay.

328
00:16:00,385 --> 00:16:01,394
I’ll see you outside.

329
00:16:15,543 --> 00:16:16,335
Oh.

330
00:16:17,642 --> 00:16:18,899
Where are you going to study?

331
00:16:22,251 --> 00:16:23,284
Over there.

332
00:16:23,284 --> 00:16:24,471
It should be nice and cool.

333
00:16:24,471 --> 00:16:25,232
Where’s Hem?

334
00:16:25,232 --> 00:16:25,882
You know Hem.

335
00:16:26,121 --> 00:16:28,307
He’s the kind of person
who puts his friends first.

336
00:16:29,042 --> 00:16:29,656
Ah.

337
00:16:29,656 --> 00:16:31,600
Where’s Cheewa?

338
00:16:33,059 --> 00:16:33,922
Is he changing?

339
00:16:33,922 --> 00:16:34,422
Yeah.

340
00:16:35,663 --> 00:16:36,756
He’s in the changing room.

341
00:16:36,908 --> 00:16:38,066
Will he know how to wear the uniform?

342
00:16:38,349 --> 00:16:39,279
He should be out soon.

343
00:16:39,388 --> 00:16:40,827
How many hours have you practiced?

344
00:16:40,827 --> 00:16:42,617
I don’t know how many,

345
00:16:44,010 --> 00:16:45,723
but all the juniors have gone home.

346
00:16:45,723 --> 00:16:47,181
I don’t have a practice partner anymore,

347
00:16:47,312 --> 00:16:50,005
so I’ll just count teaching Cheewa
as practice.

348
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:51,738
Okay, then.

349
00:16:51,825 --> 00:16:53,167
We’re going to study now.

350
00:16:53,167 --> 00:16:53,842
Mm.

351
00:16:54,103 --> 00:16:54,729
See you later.

352
00:16:54,729 --> 00:16:55,451
See you.

353
00:16:55,451 --> 00:16:56,124
We’re off.

354
00:17:09,792 --> 00:17:10,471
Why don’t you take your glasses off?

355
00:17:10,471 --> 00:17:11,322
You don’t want to break them.

356
00:17:12,585 --> 00:17:13,758
I won’t fall.

357
00:17:13,758 --> 00:17:15,378
Wow.

358
00:17:15,378 --> 00:17:16,589
You’re confident, huh?

359
00:17:17,547 --> 00:17:18,291
Yeah.

360
00:17:19,202 --> 00:17:20,934
Your friends aren’t coming?

361
00:17:21,202 --> 00:17:22,418
If they want to learn too, it’s okay.

362
00:17:22,418 --> 00:17:23,333
I’ll teach you guys together.

363
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:25,261
Jomyut and Newton came to school today,

364
00:17:25,261 --> 00:17:27,181
but I think they went straight to our club.

365
00:17:27,181 --> 00:17:28,261
They’re not coming here.

366
00:17:28,722 --> 00:17:31,682
The Astronomy Club has an activity today?

367
00:17:32,030 --> 00:17:32,817
Yes.

368
00:17:33,056 --> 00:17:36,216
We’re building something to find aliens.

369
00:17:36,216 --> 00:17:36,822
What do you mean?

370
00:17:37,018 --> 00:17:39,464
It’ll take a while to explain.

371
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:40,710
Then you don’t have to.

372
00:17:47,350 --> 00:17:48,555
What do I have to do?

373
00:17:53,239 --> 00:17:54,323
You look promising.

374
00:17:55,673 --> 00:17:56,751
I’m just prepared.

375
00:17:57,469 --> 00:17:59,215
Don’t get ahead of yourself, kid.

376
00:17:59,868 --> 00:18:01,157
Come on. Let’s warm up.

377
00:18:01,157 --> 00:18:01,884
Follow me.

378
00:18:03,255 --> 00:18:04,121
Neck first.

379
00:18:07,147 --> 00:18:07,833
Stretch it out.

380
00:18:12,242 --> 00:18:12,957
Why are you smiling?

381
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:14,951
I’m just smiling.

382
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:21,499
You’re not supposed to touch my hands.

383
00:18:21,499 --> 00:18:22,452
Just hold out yours.

384
00:18:22,452 --> 00:18:23,366
Do it.

385
00:18:24,242 --> 00:18:25,015
Lean over too.

386
00:18:25,668 --> 00:18:26,362
Yeah.

387
00:18:27,255 --> 00:18:28,063
Very good.

388
00:18:28,063 --> 00:18:28,712
Okay.

389
00:18:29,953 --> 00:18:32,230
Woo! Come on!

390
00:18:32,578 --> 00:18:33,877
You didn’t have to say that.

391
00:18:33,877 --> 00:18:34,938
You didn’t have to say that.

392
00:18:35,308 --> 00:18:36,115
Gosh!

393
00:18:36,986 --> 00:18:38,112
Have you done judo before?

394
00:18:39,353 --> 00:18:40,300
A little bit.

395
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:41,488
But I’ve forgotten it all.

396
00:18:41,488 --> 00:18:43,168
Let’s start with how to stand.

397
00:18:43,168 --> 00:18:44,336
Legs apart.

398
00:18:44,336 --> 00:18:45,961
Not too wide. Not too narrow.

399
00:18:46,162 --> 00:18:48,158
Mm. You’re quick in the head.

400
00:18:49,754 --> 00:18:50,635
What’s that?

401
00:18:50,635 --> 00:18:51,805
My head’s quick.

402
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:53,586
Ugh.

403
00:18:54,442 --> 00:18:55,311
Ugh.

404
00:18:58,838 --> 00:18:59,507
Huh?

405
00:19:00,334 --> 00:19:03,137
I’ve read somewhere

406
00:19:03,572 --> 00:19:06,799
that if you like someone,
you should mess with them often.

407
00:19:11,327 --> 00:19:12,463
Let’s start with this.

408
00:19:12,702 --> 00:19:13,821
Show respect to your opponent.

409
00:19:18,697 --> 00:19:19,871
What are you doing the Wai for?

410
00:19:20,938 --> 00:19:22,022
You.

411
00:19:22,544 --> 00:19:23,424
Why?

412
00:19:24,491 --> 00:19:25,543
To show respect.

413
00:19:28,678 --> 00:19:30,030
Give it a try.

414
00:19:30,770 --> 00:19:31,538
Yes, correct.

415
00:19:31,538 --> 00:19:32,233
Yeah.

416
00:19:32,233 --> 00:19:33,411
Good form.

417
00:19:33,411 --> 00:19:34,606
You know how to grab now, right?

418
00:19:34,737 --> 00:19:36,203
Now, when you actually go for the grab,

419
00:19:36,399 --> 00:19:38,150
you need to knock their hand away
so they can’t grab you.

420
00:19:38,150 --> 00:19:38,844
For example,

421
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:39,804
try to grab me.

422
00:19:40,326 --> 00:19:41,716
Like this. Then grab.

423
00:19:41,716 --> 00:19:42,985
One. Two. Three.

424
00:19:43,834 --> 00:19:44,955
Cheewa.

425
00:19:49,853 --> 00:19:50,597
One.

426
00:19:50,749 --> 00:19:51,747
Two. Three.

427
00:19:53,293 --> 00:19:54,481
Yes. That’s right.

428
00:19:54,481 --> 00:19:55,110
Yeah.

429
00:19:56,242 --> 00:19:58,911
Yes. Great job.

430
00:19:59,368 --> 00:20:00,590
Same grip as before.

431
00:20:02,353 --> 00:20:03,277
You grab me too.

432
00:20:03,930 --> 00:20:05,271
Where? Yes.

433
00:20:06,098 --> 00:20:07,058
Bend down.

434
00:20:08,103 --> 00:20:09,334
Not yet.

435
00:20:09,813 --> 00:20:10,622
Bend down.

436
00:20:11,638 --> 00:20:12,242
Then do this.

437
00:20:12,242 --> 00:20:12,742
Mm.

438
00:20:12,981 --> 00:20:13,731
And this.

439
00:20:15,168 --> 00:20:15,749
Okay?

440
00:20:15,749 --> 00:20:16,249
Okay.

441
00:20:16,249 --> 00:20:16,749
Okay.

442
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:18,444
Right here.

443
00:20:19,097 --> 00:20:21,622
Then, for the second part,
wrap your arms around the waist.

444
00:20:22,776 --> 00:20:24,042
Get ready.

445
00:20:24,042 --> 00:20:24,925
Then come up.

446
00:20:25,665 --> 00:20:26,874
And throw, okay?

447
00:20:26,874 --> 00:20:27,374
Okay.

448
00:20:27,374 --> 00:20:28,045
Can you do it?

449
00:20:28,045 --> 00:20:28,545
Yeah.

450
00:20:28,763 --> 00:20:29,467
Can you do it?

451
00:20:29,577 --> 00:20:30,078
Yeah.

452
00:20:30,448 --> 00:20:31,607
Alright, try throwing me.

453
00:20:32,652 --> 00:20:33,387
Bend down.

454
00:20:33,387 --> 00:20:34,018
Bend down now.

455
00:20:34,410 --> 00:20:35,679
Then use your hand.

456
00:20:36,242 --> 00:20:36,742
Yes.

457
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:37,630
There.

458
00:20:37,978 --> 00:20:38,948
Hold on to the waist.

459
00:20:40,036 --> 00:20:41,698
Then use your hip… your hip.

460
00:20:41,698 --> 00:20:43,215
Yes. That’s right. Hup!

461
00:20:43,302 --> 00:20:44,454
Then lean into it.

462
00:20:44,454 --> 00:20:45,768
Yeah! Awesome!

463
00:20:46,051 --> 00:20:46,742
Can you do it?

464
00:20:46,938 --> 00:20:47,438
Yes.

465
00:20:47,438 --> 00:20:47,938
Okay.

466
00:20:47,938 --> 00:20:48,438
Try one more time.

467
00:20:58,234 --> 00:20:59,691
You just had to copy me, huh?

468
00:21:12,098 --> 00:21:13,173
Why are you lying like that?

469
00:21:13,978 --> 00:21:15,780
It’s comfortable.

470
00:21:15,780 --> 00:21:18,443
Hey, you said you’ve learned a lot of sports.

471
00:21:18,726 --> 00:21:19,937
You did judo too, right?

472
00:21:21,047 --> 00:21:21,775
Yes.

473
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:25,131
No wonder you have
a really good foundation.

474
00:21:25,131 --> 00:21:26,562
Do you remember any moves?

475
00:21:26,823 --> 00:21:28,641
I actually didn’t remember anything.

476
00:21:29,050 --> 00:21:32,050
But once you taught me, I remember.

477
00:21:33,443 --> 00:21:35,746
Really?

478
00:21:36,617 --> 00:21:38,520
Oh, you’re good.

479
00:21:38,803 --> 00:21:39,578
Yeah.

480
00:21:39,992 --> 00:21:42,119
But can you see without your glasses?

481
00:21:46,865 --> 00:21:48,394
I was actually just messing with you.

482
00:21:48,721 --> 00:21:51,433
I put on contact lenses in the changing room.

483
00:21:52,304 --> 00:21:54,205
I was waiting to see if you’d say anything.

484
00:21:55,642 --> 00:21:57,072
Thank you for pointing it out.

485
00:21:57,703 --> 00:22:00,809
It means you pay
quite a bit of attention to me.

486
00:22:02,072 --> 00:22:02,798
Mm.

487
00:22:06,847 --> 00:22:09,063
But after learning judo with you,

488
00:22:09,194 --> 00:22:10,572
I’ll take them out.

489
00:22:11,007 --> 00:22:12,442
I’m more used to wearing glasses.

490
00:22:13,052 --> 00:22:13,842
Mm.

491
00:22:14,713 --> 00:22:15,818
And…

492
00:22:16,645 --> 00:22:18,181
one more thing.

493
00:22:20,122 --> 00:22:22,887
I’m worried you won’t be used to
how cool I look.

494
00:22:29,799 --> 00:22:31,209
Who taught you that? Tell me.

495
00:22:38,524 --> 00:22:39,649
Never mind. Let’s continue.

496
00:22:40,634 --> 00:22:41,380
Come on.

497
00:22:41,984 --> 00:22:42,761
You’re impossible.

498
00:22:52,259 --> 00:22:54,045
This weather is so damn perfect for sleeping.

499
00:22:54,362 --> 00:22:55,057
Yeah.

500
00:23:01,936 --> 00:23:03,408
Here I am, boys.

501
00:23:06,202 --> 00:23:06,848
What?

502
00:23:07,602 --> 00:23:08,672
Did I miss something?

503
00:23:08,672 --> 00:23:10,131
What time did we say we’d meet?

504
00:23:11,263 --> 00:23:12,881
Come on.

505
00:23:12,881 --> 00:23:14,242
Look. It’s raining.

506
00:23:14,242 --> 00:23:15,468
No excuses.

507
00:23:15,577 --> 00:23:17,083
Don’t even try that.

508
00:23:17,083 --> 00:23:18,783
You should be glad I even made it here.

509
00:23:18,783 --> 00:23:20,070
It’s raining.

510
00:23:20,331 --> 00:23:21,514
I’m hungry.

511
00:23:21,514 --> 00:23:23,016
Yeah, exactly.

512
00:23:23,122 --> 00:23:23,872
By the way,

513
00:23:23,872 --> 00:23:25,693
where are Jomyut and Newton?

514
00:23:25,693 --> 00:23:26,802
My beloved brothers.

515
00:23:26,802 --> 00:23:29,416
Those two are experimenting
with a device to find aliens.

516
00:23:29,416 --> 00:23:31,743
You guys can check it out after you eat
if you’re interested.

517
00:23:31,743 --> 00:23:33,048
I’ll take you.

518
00:23:33,527 --> 00:23:34,902
Hem, where did you get that shirt?

519
00:23:35,642 --> 00:23:37,888
Oh, it was hanging over there,

520
00:23:37,888 --> 00:23:39,520
so I put it on. It looks good on me.

521
00:23:39,781 --> 00:23:40,744
Hey, hey, hey!

522
00:23:42,242 --> 00:23:42,962
Argh!

523
00:23:43,228 --> 00:23:44,847
Well, since he’s already down…

524
00:23:44,847 --> 00:23:45,860
Damn.

525
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:47,998
I’m just late.

526
00:23:47,998 --> 00:23:49,227
Hey, don’t hurt him.

527
00:23:51,382 --> 00:23:52,165
What are you going to do?

528
00:23:52,165 --> 00:23:52,704
This.

529
00:23:58,190 --> 00:23:59,813
Do you guys want to go up?

530
00:24:02,426 --> 00:24:03,530
I think…

531
00:24:04,531 --> 00:24:05,729
I’m not full yet.

532
00:24:06,012 --> 00:24:06,987
I’ll be right back.

533
00:24:07,792 --> 00:24:10,109
Oh, I’m going home to bring in the laundry.

534
00:24:10,109 --> 00:24:11,267
Yeah.

535
00:24:18,981 --> 00:24:19,736
Let’s go.

536
00:24:20,062 --> 00:24:21,155
We’re all here anyway.

537
00:24:23,833 --> 00:24:24,532
Right?

538
00:24:26,056 --> 00:24:26,956
Mm.

539
00:24:28,132 --> 00:24:29,162
Lead the way, Cheewa.

540
00:24:32,209 --> 00:24:33,289
Lead the way.

541
00:24:35,656 --> 00:24:36,757
Come on, you two.

542
00:24:37,127 --> 00:24:37,824
You lead the way.

543
00:24:37,824 --> 00:24:38,613
No, I don’t want you to run away.

544
00:24:39,745 --> 00:24:40,561
Damn it.

545
00:24:41,345 --> 00:24:42,307
You’re forcing us to do this.

546
00:24:43,402 --> 00:24:44,787
What if I get a stomach ulcer?

547
00:24:44,787 --> 00:24:45,875
Want me to throw you?

548
00:24:47,116 --> 00:24:48,366
Good job, buddy.

549
00:24:48,823 --> 00:24:52,112
Thara, teach your friends to talk like you
and keep quiet.

550
00:24:54,038 --> 00:24:56,324
According to the numbers, which never lie,

551
00:24:56,324 --> 00:24:59,624
when you discover aliens, they usually reveal
themselves for no longer than two minutes.

552
00:24:59,624 --> 00:25:02,601
That means every step we take
as we explore this building counts.

553
00:25:14,628 --> 00:25:15,388
Are we there yet?

554
00:25:17,370 --> 00:25:21,853
Why do I feel like there’s some weird energy
radiating from the club room?

555
00:25:25,287 --> 00:25:26,152
Holy shit, Niran.

556
00:25:26,530 --> 00:25:27,785
I’m getting goosebumps.

557
00:25:28,662 --> 00:25:29,922
It’s really powerful.

558
00:25:30,013 --> 00:25:31,036
I think we should leave.

559
00:25:31,505 --> 00:25:32,668
Yeah, let’s go.

560
00:25:32,668 --> 00:25:34,609
It’s a normal bodily response

561
00:25:34,942 --> 00:25:37,781
when the skin is exposed to
sudden changes in the air.

562
00:25:37,781 --> 00:25:41,147
The nervous system signals tiny muscles
at the hair roots, making them stand up.

563
00:25:43,710 --> 00:25:44,838
What’s he talking about?

564
00:25:45,685 --> 00:25:46,779
Keep it short.

565
00:25:46,915 --> 00:25:47,586
I’m dumb.

566
00:25:49,084 --> 00:25:50,129
It’s the AC.

567
00:25:52,353 --> 00:25:53,980
It’s the air from the AC in that room.

568
00:25:57,611 --> 00:25:58,540
Is it clear now?

569
00:25:58,879 --> 00:26:00,747
It’s the AC, you idiot.

570
00:26:01,685 --> 00:26:04,860
Hey, weren’t you just scared like me?

571
00:26:07,326 --> 00:26:10,955
Perfect timing, members from planet CW101.

572
00:26:11,681 --> 00:26:15,935
The members from the other planets
have finished building the alien detector.

573
00:26:16,026 --> 00:26:17,802
We’re going to test it in the building tonight.

574
00:26:17,802 --> 00:26:18,742
Hold on.

575
00:26:19,196 --> 00:26:21,404
About the members from the other planets…

576
00:26:22,781 --> 00:26:23,769
Fine, I won’t question it.

577
00:26:23,879 --> 00:26:26,119
But are you really going to
look for aliens tonight?

578
00:26:26,422 --> 00:26:27,738
It has to be tonight.

579
00:26:28,116 --> 00:26:30,040
According to the numbers, which never lie,

580
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:33,555
when you discover aliens, they usually reveal
themselves for no longer than two minutes.

581
00:26:33,676 --> 00:26:36,570
That means every step we take
as we explore this building counts.

582
00:26:36,767 --> 00:26:39,435
Who knows? The ghost rumored to be
in the science building

583
00:26:39,753 --> 00:26:42,708
could be an alien hiding in our school.

584
00:26:42,708 --> 00:26:44,996
The Astronomy Club needs to prove it.

585
00:26:45,147 --> 00:26:48,061
Will our four new explorers be joining us?

586
00:26:48,379 --> 00:26:49,735
What planet are you guys from?

587
00:26:52,337 --> 00:26:53,432
Planet Namek.

588
00:26:55,490 --> 00:26:56,214
Uh…

589
00:26:56,849 --> 00:26:59,639
Can you talk normally, bro?

590
00:26:59,790 --> 00:27:00,343
Okay?

591
00:27:01,190 --> 00:27:02,163
Use normal language.

592
00:27:02,163 --> 00:27:05,463
Hmm… do you want to join us, seniors?

593
00:27:05,902 --> 00:27:07,547
Pretty please.

594
00:27:07,865 --> 00:27:10,621
P’Thipok, P’Thara, P’Hem,
please come with us.

595
00:27:12,315 --> 00:27:14,654
You guys go ahead.

596
00:27:14,654 --> 00:27:16,693
I hope you find them soon.

597
00:27:17,797 --> 00:27:18,465
Right?

598
00:27:18,465 --> 00:27:19,175
Right?

599
00:27:19,947 --> 00:27:20,954
That’s right.

600
00:27:20,954 --> 00:27:21,483
Yeah.

601
00:27:21,483 --> 00:27:25,690
By the way, does anyone have time
to take us downstairs?

602
00:27:25,690 --> 00:27:27,351
Right. Before it gets dark.

603
00:27:27,699 --> 00:27:28,980
Yeah. We should go before it gets dark.

604
00:27:33,352 --> 00:27:34,986
Oh, it’s already dark.

605
00:27:35,304 --> 00:27:39,437
Guys, I feel cold, just like when I was
in the air-conditioned room earlier.

606
00:27:40,345 --> 00:27:42,245
Yeah, me too.

607
00:27:43,138 --> 00:27:44,491
I think we should leave.

608
00:27:44,673 --> 00:27:46,103
Let’s stick together going down the stairs.

609
00:27:46,390 --> 00:27:47,487
No splitting up.

610
00:27:48,213 --> 00:27:49,157
Heads up.

611
00:27:49,157 --> 00:27:50,996
If any of you makes noise,
I’ll kick you.

612
00:27:51,178 --> 00:27:53,826
No brotherhood. No friendship whatsoever.

613
00:27:55,097 --> 00:27:56,515
Don’t come any closer!

614
00:27:56,878 --> 00:27:57,618
Hem!

615
00:27:59,312 --> 00:28:00,271
Thara just sneezed.

616
00:28:00,468 --> 00:28:01,240
Stop being dramatic.

617
00:28:01,603 --> 00:28:03,327
Sorry. I’m allergic to dust.

618
00:28:03,735 --> 00:28:05,078
Where are you guys going?

619
00:28:05,744 --> 00:28:07,378
Aren’t you coming to explore
the science building with us?

620
00:28:07,923 --> 00:28:09,223
If we find aliens,

621
00:28:09,223 --> 00:28:12,370
that’ll be a very important discovery
for humankind.

622
00:28:12,370 --> 00:28:14,377
To hell with humankind.

623
00:28:14,377 --> 00:28:16,647
Right now, you guys have to
take me downstairs.

624
00:28:16,768 --> 00:28:17,756
We’ll all go.

625
00:28:18,013 --> 00:28:19,951
I’ll come back and kick anyone
who doesn’t come.

626
00:28:19,951 --> 00:28:21,086
Yeah, let’s go.

627
00:28:21,601 --> 00:28:22,101
Shit!

628
00:28:22,374 --> 00:28:23,121
Shit!

629
00:28:23,620 --> 00:28:24,590
Stay with us.

630
00:28:24,938 --> 00:28:27,861
This discovery will be recorded as our group
being the first students to make it.

631
00:28:28,879 --> 00:28:29,624
Hey, what?

632
00:28:29,624 --> 00:28:30,574
What are you doing?

633
00:28:30,574 --> 00:28:31,939
What? Help me.

634
00:28:32,121 --> 00:28:33,502
You look suspicious, P’Hem.

635
00:28:33,788 --> 00:28:35,907
Are you one of the aliens?

636
00:28:36,830 --> 00:28:38,099
We brought the detector.

637
00:28:38,674 --> 00:28:41,232
You two seem way more like aliens than I do.

638
00:28:41,459 --> 00:28:42,834
Have you checked yourselves?

639
00:28:45,678 --> 00:28:46,917
Do you want to leave now?

640
00:28:47,189 --> 00:28:48,667
I’ll walk you down.

641
00:28:49,272 --> 00:28:50,443
Aren’t you leaving with us?

642
00:28:51,003 --> 00:28:51,748
No.

643
00:28:51,990 --> 00:28:54,307
I’m exploring with the other club members.

644
00:29:06,535 --> 00:29:07,177
Okay.

645
00:29:07,767 --> 00:29:08,495
We’ll stay.

646
00:29:10,371 --> 00:29:10,900
Huh?

647
00:29:11,883 --> 00:29:13,267
We’ll stay.

648
00:29:14,281 --> 00:29:15,556
Why the hell would you stay?

649
00:29:15,859 --> 00:29:17,068
Shit, Hem. Your spit!

650
00:29:18,218 --> 00:29:19,892
We’ll look for aliens, of course.

651
00:29:21,874 --> 00:29:22,851
Don’t you believe in it?

652
00:29:23,788 --> 00:29:25,063
Shit!
What the hell?

653
00:29:25,063 --> 00:29:25,855
Sorry. It’s the dust.

654
00:29:25,856 --> 00:29:26,537
Want some medicine?

655
00:29:26,536 --> 00:29:28,205
Hem, Thara just sneezed
for the second time.

656
00:29:28,205 --> 00:29:30,672
Wait, is P’Thara an alien too?

657
00:29:30,672 --> 00:29:31,786
My eyes sting.

658
00:29:32,210 --> 00:29:33,208
Please hold your arms out.

659
00:29:34,599 --> 00:29:35,556
Arms up.

660
00:29:36,267 --> 00:29:36,859
Yeah.

661
00:29:36,996 --> 00:29:37,885
Turn around for me.

662
00:29:37,885 --> 00:29:38,515
Turn around.

663
00:29:41,072 --> 00:29:41,850
Okay.

664
00:29:41,971 --> 00:29:43,350
You’re not an alien.

665
00:29:43,350 --> 00:29:46,588
No, I’m an alien.

666
00:29:46,664 --> 00:29:49,137
Please kill me and dump me downstairs.

667
00:29:49,137 --> 00:29:49,836
Check again.

668
00:29:49,912 --> 00:29:50,605
Check again.

669
00:29:56,832 --> 00:29:57,458
Go!

670
00:29:57,609 --> 00:29:58,783
Shit. Where are we going?

671
00:29:58,783 --> 00:29:59,871
Hurry.

672
00:30:00,007 --> 00:30:01,013
Hem, come on.

673
00:30:01,512 --> 00:30:02,214
Geez.

674
00:30:06,223 --> 00:30:07,351
Are we seriously doing this?

675
00:30:07,971 --> 00:30:09,732
Of course. We’ve come this far already.

676
00:30:09,974 --> 00:30:11,051
Shit, guys.

677
00:30:11,051 --> 00:30:12,347
Can we go down?

678
00:30:12,347 --> 00:30:13,443
Let the juniors explore.

679
00:30:13,879 --> 00:30:15,025
We don’t have anything to do with this, do we?

680
00:30:15,494 --> 00:30:17,072
I’m worried about Cheewa and Jomyut.

681
00:30:18,055 --> 00:30:20,371
It’s better to have at least one senior
with them than none at all.

682
00:30:20,371 --> 00:30:21,295
Oh, for God’s sake.

683
00:30:21,507 --> 00:30:23,366
Is now really the time to be acting cool?

684
00:30:23,684 --> 00:30:24,967
Why don’t you guys go home?

685
00:30:25,224 --> 00:30:27,092
No. If you’re not going down, how could we?

686
00:30:28,227 --> 00:30:29,194
Then stay together.

687
00:30:29,194 --> 00:30:30,778
The ghost in the science building isn’t real.

688
00:30:31,504 --> 00:30:32,360
Hey, Niran.

689
00:30:32,436 --> 00:30:33,934
Slap yourself in the mouth right now.

690
00:30:33,934 --> 00:30:35,049
You’re not supposed to disrespect it.

691
00:30:35,503 --> 00:30:36,571
I’m not disrespecting it.

692
00:30:36,571 --> 00:30:38,027
I just think it isn’t real.

693
00:30:46,539 --> 00:30:47,257
What?

694
00:30:47,257 --> 00:30:48,576
I think it’s unusually cold.

695
00:30:49,393 --> 00:30:50,660
I’ve got goosebumps all over.

696
00:30:51,053 --> 00:30:51,718
Ugh.

697
00:30:53,879 --> 00:30:56,387
You guys can wait in the club room.

698
00:30:57,083 --> 00:30:57,930
Yeah.

699
00:30:57,930 --> 00:31:00,668
I think that’s a pretty good idea.

700
00:31:01,818 --> 00:31:03,029
Good idea, my ass!

701
00:31:03,423 --> 00:31:04,908
I can stay with you.

702
00:31:05,876 --> 00:31:07,095
No, Cheewa.

703
00:31:07,307 --> 00:31:09,130
I know how much you love
astronomy and space.

704
00:31:09,130 --> 00:31:10,673
You can’t miss looking for aliens.

705
00:31:10,673 --> 00:31:11,173
I’m coming with you.

706
00:31:12,762 --> 00:31:13,793
Damn it!

707
00:31:13,879 --> 00:31:15,360
Someone, please tell me.

708
00:31:15,466 --> 00:31:17,488
Who let Niran make all decisions like this?

709
00:31:18,139 --> 00:31:19,505
Let’s keep going then.

710
00:31:21,668 --> 00:31:23,415
Hey, do you want to reconsider?

711
00:31:24,701 --> 00:31:26,132
Hem, watch it!

712
00:31:27,327 --> 00:31:28,205
Hem, you’re going to tear my shirt.

713
00:31:28,205 --> 00:31:29,512
Well, I’m scared!

714
00:31:29,829 --> 00:31:30,329
Ugh.

715
00:31:31,842 --> 00:31:32,736
That room.

716
00:31:35,595 --> 00:31:37,488
Look at you, shaking like crazy.

717
00:31:39,620 --> 00:31:40,348
Hem.

718
00:31:41,181 --> 00:31:42,766
Now this is some real goosebumps.

719
00:31:43,189 --> 00:31:44,841
F*ck. Don’t say that.

720
00:31:49,045 --> 00:31:50,712
I’m scared.

721
00:31:53,133 --> 00:31:53,764
I’ll do it.

722
00:31:54,540 --> 00:31:55,641
Shit. Thara’s doing it.

723
00:32:03,030 --> 00:32:04,205
Shit, it’s not locked.

724
00:32:04,765 --> 00:32:05,674
That scared me.

725
00:32:06,007 --> 00:32:07,365
Don’t you guys want to find out?

726
00:32:07,758 --> 00:32:08,548
Go in.

727
00:32:17,277 --> 00:32:18,162
Can I ask you something?

728
00:32:18,737 --> 00:32:20,338
Why do you like astronomy?

729
00:32:20,535 --> 00:32:22,416
How did you know
you liked it that much?

730
00:32:22,416 --> 00:32:23,734
Are you scared, P’Niran?

731
00:32:24,823 --> 00:32:26,369
I’m so excited.

732
00:32:42,852 --> 00:32:43,563
Whoa!

733
00:32:43,563 --> 00:32:44,763
Aliens! Aliens! Aliens!

734
00:32:50,016 --> 00:32:51,024
My glasses are gone.

735
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:53,858
My glasses are gone.

736
00:32:53,858 --> 00:32:54,619
Let’s go!

737
00:32:55,236 --> 00:32:57,233
My legs are frozen. I can’t move.

738
00:32:57,233 --> 00:32:57,998
Let go of me!

739
00:32:59,881 --> 00:33:01,552
I pissed myself.

740
00:33:02,606 --> 00:33:03,543
Let go!

741
00:33:07,193 --> 00:33:08,719
Shit. What are we doing?

742
00:33:08,719 --> 00:33:10,878
I’m done. I’m freaking done.

743
00:33:10,878 --> 00:33:12,193
I’m freaking done.

744
00:33:12,193 --> 00:33:12,880
I want to go home.

745
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:14,068
Get a grip, Pok.

746
00:33:14,859 --> 00:33:16,690
Let’s get out of here.

747
00:33:16,690 --> 00:33:19,340
What if we run into those aliens?

748
00:33:20,376 --> 00:33:22,375
Hem’s definitely been eaten.

749
00:33:29,526 --> 00:33:32,660
Oh, shit. Namo tassa bhagavato.

750
00:33:32,660 --> 00:33:34,585
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sammā-sambuddhassa.

751
00:33:34,585 --> 00:33:36,165
Can you be quiet? They’re going to hear us.

752
00:33:36,749 --> 00:33:39,696
Do you really think aliens are going to be
afraid of your chanting?

753
00:33:40,336 --> 00:33:42,745
Can’t you freaking see
there are four of them?

754
00:33:42,851 --> 00:33:44,602
F*ck. What do we do?

755
00:33:49,235 --> 00:33:50,043
Ugh.

756
00:33:50,513 --> 00:33:51,050
Hello.

757
00:33:51,050 --> 00:33:51,898
Hello, Teacher.

758
00:33:51,898 --> 00:33:53,281
Hold these for me.

759
00:33:54,750 --> 00:33:58,393
You should’ve told us
you were going to look for stuff in that room.

760
00:33:58,393 --> 00:34:00,473
I was just getting the costume.

761
00:34:00,473 --> 00:34:01,908
Why were you being all sneaky about it?

762
00:34:02,096 --> 00:34:02,804
Who?

763
00:34:03,388 --> 00:34:04,259
Who was being sneaky?

764
00:34:04,598 --> 00:34:06,607
Who was being suspicious? No one.

765
00:34:06,607 --> 00:34:07,319
I was acting normal.

766
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,910
What are you going to do with all this stuff?

767
00:34:13,507 --> 00:34:14,564
Don’t tell anyone.

768
00:34:15,054 --> 00:34:16,229
I’m filming a clip.

769
00:34:17,531 --> 00:34:18,391
At home.

770
00:34:18,730 --> 00:34:19,689
It’s embarrassing.

771
00:34:21,134 --> 00:34:22,193
I’m embarrassed.

772
00:34:22,897 --> 00:34:24,338
Are you going to keep talking all night?

773
00:34:25,106 --> 00:34:26,516
I want to change my pants.

774
00:34:29,943 --> 00:34:30,788
Damn it.

775
00:34:30,788 --> 00:34:32,457
My life as a musician.

776
00:34:32,457 --> 00:34:33,964
I can’t believe I got so scared
and peed myself.

777
00:34:34,699 --> 00:34:35,466
Damn.

778
00:34:40,112 --> 00:34:41,194
Whatever happens, happens. You in?

779
00:34:43,548 --> 00:34:44,703
Yeah, let’s do it.

780
00:34:47,358 --> 00:34:49,771
What the f*ck?!

781
00:34:49,771 --> 00:34:51,771
No.

782
00:34:53,089 --> 00:34:53,834
It’s the head model.

783
00:34:55,523 --> 00:34:56,306
Sorry.

784
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:57,127
You idiot.

785
00:34:57,579 --> 00:34:59,099
You scared the hell out of me.

786
00:35:00,199 --> 00:35:00,935
For real this time.

787
00:35:02,065 --> 00:35:02,675
One.

788
00:35:03,108 --> 00:35:03,825
Two.

789
00:35:03,825 --> 00:35:04,440
Three!

790
00:35:07,812 --> 00:35:09,803
Ghost!

791
00:35:15,227 --> 00:35:16,089
Sorry.

792
00:35:16,089 --> 00:35:16,807
Slow down.

793
00:35:18,351 --> 00:35:19,328
You can’t see clearly, right?

794
00:35:20,353 --> 00:35:21,806
Sorry, I made you run a little too fast.

795
00:35:23,713 --> 00:35:26,491
Do you want me to go back up
and find the glasses you dropped?

796
00:35:27,037 --> 00:35:28,172
Oh, it’s fine.

797
00:35:28,662 --> 00:35:31,443
Someone from the club will probably
keep them for me.

798
00:35:31,473 --> 00:35:32,784
I can get them later.

799
00:35:34,084 --> 00:35:34,860
Okay.

800
00:35:36,084 --> 00:35:37,388
You’re not hurt, right?

801
00:35:39,159 --> 00:35:39,904
Hold on to me.

802
00:35:43,708 --> 00:35:44,752
Hold on to the wall.

803
00:35:44,752 --> 00:35:45,252
Okay.

804
00:35:46,646 --> 00:35:48,565
Careful. Watch your steps.

805
00:35:48,565 --> 00:35:49,438
Easy.

806
00:35:52,790 --> 00:35:53,975
That run was exhausting, huh?

807
00:35:55,840 --> 00:35:56,679
Sit down.

808
00:36:01,689 --> 00:36:02,553
Are you okay?

809
00:36:06,033 --> 00:36:07,376
Are you scared, P’Niran?

810
00:36:09,956 --> 00:36:11,397
I actually was at first.

811
00:36:11,962 --> 00:36:12,847
But not anymore.

812
00:36:15,634 --> 00:36:18,082
I’m so excited.

813
00:36:19,457 --> 00:36:20,141
Huh?

814
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:23,362
Is that the face of someone who’s excited
because they’ve seen aliens?

815
00:36:24,624 --> 00:36:26,527
I’m not talking about aliens.

816
00:36:28,938 --> 00:36:32,506
I’m talking about being with you.

817
00:36:39,173 --> 00:36:40,277
Yeah, I believe you.

818
00:36:44,889 --> 00:36:45,834
I’m sorry.

819
00:36:48,471 --> 00:36:50,740
It’s a bodily reaction.

820
00:36:53,810 --> 00:36:54,527
Wanna keep holding it?

821
00:37:01,756 --> 00:37:02,557
I’m kidding.

822
00:37:09,687 --> 00:37:10,953
There are so many stars tonight.

823
00:37:16,972 --> 00:37:17,710
Yes.

824
00:37:18,275 --> 00:37:22,463
Sometimes, Teacher Boriboon would
take us outside, point out the stars,
and tell us their names.

825
00:37:27,830 --> 00:37:29,555
Oh, then it’s a shame

826
00:37:29,969 --> 00:37:30,987
you can’t see them today.

827
00:37:33,209 --> 00:37:34,875
How are you going to tell me
the names of the stars?

828
00:37:36,113 --> 00:37:38,099
It’s okay. I remember them.

829
00:37:38,438 --> 00:37:40,636
Just describe what they look like.

830
00:37:41,182 --> 00:37:41,960
Whoa.

831
00:37:42,675 --> 00:37:43,664
That’ll be hard.

832
00:37:46,904 --> 00:37:47,552
Give it a try.

833
00:37:53,448 --> 00:37:54,018
Okay.

834
00:37:55,035 --> 00:37:56,070
Uh…

835
00:37:57,595 --> 00:38:03,092
There are three stars in a straight line.

836
00:38:03,313 --> 00:38:04,240
Orion’s Belt.

837
00:38:04,654 --> 00:38:05,921
Wait, is that right?

838
00:38:06,580 --> 00:38:07,143
Yes.

839
00:38:09,158 --> 00:38:10,480
Alright, if you say so.

840
00:38:11,214 --> 00:38:12,272
Hmm…

841
00:38:13,025 --> 00:38:14,309
Which one should I pick?

842
00:38:16,211 --> 00:38:16,961
Ah.

843
00:38:18,053 --> 00:38:20,835
It’s a group of seven stars.

844
00:38:24,602 --> 00:38:25,638
What constellation is that?

845
00:38:28,501 --> 00:38:29,348
The Pleiades.

846
00:38:30,177 --> 00:38:31,354
Ah.

847
00:38:31,354 --> 00:38:33,485
Is that the one with the story about

848
00:38:34,351 --> 00:38:36,630
seven chicks jumping into a fire?

849
00:38:37,459 --> 00:38:38,201
Yes.

850
00:38:38,540 --> 00:38:39,666
Mm.

851
00:38:43,150 --> 00:38:44,102
Whoa.

852
00:38:45,307 --> 00:38:46,273
There are so many more.

853
00:38:46,386 --> 00:38:47,193
Which one should I pick?

854
00:39:08,253 --> 00:39:09,627
I don’t have light shining out of me.

855
00:39:10,004 --> 00:39:10,900
What’s with that stare?

856
00:39:19,230 --> 00:39:20,503
Ow.

857
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:23,428
I’m sorry.

858
00:39:23,428 --> 00:39:24,751
I thought you were an alien.

859
00:39:25,956 --> 00:39:27,249
I’m sorry.

860
00:39:27,513 --> 00:39:29,370
Seriously? You thought I was an alien?

861
00:39:29,577 --> 00:39:30,916
No need to fight over who’s wrong.

862
00:39:31,161 --> 00:39:32,753
You’ll both take responsibility.

863
00:39:33,676 --> 00:39:36,565
Shall we go back to the club
and dress Teacher Boriboon’s wound?

864
00:39:36,565 --> 00:39:38,564
It’s fine. It’s not that bad.

865
00:39:38,903 --> 00:39:41,393
Uh… excuse me.

866
00:39:41,732 --> 00:39:43,005
Your head…

867
00:39:43,593 --> 00:39:44,738
There’s blood.

868
00:39:45,152 --> 00:39:45,986
Yes.

869
00:39:52,425 --> 00:39:53,626
Looks like you’ll need stitches.

870
00:39:55,222 --> 00:39:56,252
Oh, shit.

871
00:39:58,531 --> 00:39:59,125
Oh.

872
00:39:59,125 --> 00:40:00,259
What should we do, Teacher?

873
00:40:00,259 --> 00:40:00,958
Teacher.

874
00:40:00,958 --> 00:40:01,705
Teacher!

875
00:40:02,205 --> 00:40:02,705
Oh?

876
00:40:03,034 --> 00:40:03,588
Whoa.

877
00:40:03,588 --> 00:40:04,510
What should we do, Teacher?

878
00:40:06,956 --> 00:40:07,614
Hey!

879
00:40:08,518 --> 00:40:09,889
We’re in trouble!

880
00:40:10,397 --> 00:40:11,546
Let’s go, Jomyut.

881
00:40:11,546 --> 00:40:12,634
Come on!

882
00:40:13,048 --> 00:40:14,835
Not those kids again!

883
00:40:26,100 --> 00:40:26,793
Cheewa.

884
00:40:28,526 --> 00:40:29,226
Yes?

885
00:40:30,620 --> 00:40:31,608
Can I ask you something?

886
00:40:36,911 --> 00:40:38,611
Why do you like astronomy?

887
00:40:39,534 --> 00:40:40,422
And…

888
00:40:42,569 --> 00:40:44,484
How did you know
you liked it that much?

889
00:40:45,162 --> 00:40:48,087
I noticed it when we were
at the science thing together.

890
00:40:49,236 --> 00:40:52,892
Your eyes were sparkling the whole time.

891
00:40:58,184 --> 00:40:59,469
It’s nice to look at.

892
00:41:03,390 --> 00:41:04,862
Did you know?

893
00:41:05,201 --> 00:41:08,288
You’re like a newly formed star
in the Small Magellanic Cloud,

894
00:41:08,872 --> 00:41:12,785
which is a satellite galaxy of the Milky Way, about 200,000 light-years away from us?

895
00:41:13,199 --> 00:41:14,958
What about it?

896
00:41:28,326 --> 00:41:29,301
It’s cute.

897
00:41:51,066 --> 00:41:53,242
This move is called kesa-gatame.

898
00:41:58,513 --> 00:41:59,235
Are you tired?

899
00:41:59,781 --> 00:42:00,913
Do you want to practice another move?

900
00:42:02,777 --> 00:42:03,713
We can keep going.

901
00:42:05,031 --> 00:42:07,193
This move is called

902
00:42:07,720 --> 00:42:09,324
tate-shiho-gatame.

903
00:42:10,473 --> 00:42:12,400
There’s a move like this?

904
00:42:13,513 --> 00:42:14,177
Of course there is.

905
00:42:14,177 --> 00:42:14,989
How else could I do it?

906
00:42:15,433 --> 00:42:16,680
Why? You can’t breathe?

907
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:19,553
No, this is actually a good move.

908
00:42:23,073 --> 00:42:25,250
Please look after my brother.

909
00:42:25,250 --> 00:42:27,260
He doesn’t introduce me to his new friends very often.

910
00:42:27,553 --> 00:42:29,352
Why the hell did you even bring us here?

911
00:42:29,352 --> 00:42:30,296
To relax.

912
00:42:30,447 --> 00:42:33,456
Welcome to Sea Clean Camp.

913
00:42:33,456 --> 00:42:36,729
The way I'm looking at you right now can't lie.

914
00:42:36,729 --> 00:42:38,273
And I’m so worried about you.

915
00:42:38,273 --> 00:42:39,182
Here’s some water.

916
00:42:39,182 --> 00:42:40,810
Wow, Cheewa.

917
00:42:41,243 --> 00:42:42,641
They’re going stargazing.

918
00:42:42,641 --> 00:42:43,946
Do you want to come with me?

919
00:42:44,134 --> 00:42:45,751
Which star do you think suits me?
